Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:21:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Core CI: state-contract-dispatch hourly upstream
 canary + core_ref on core merges

Part 2 of the root fix for red state CI t_eeeeee0000000014 (card t_eeeeee0000000039).
Part 1 (state PR: fixture pins, mods_ref/core_ref inputs, watcher canary stream): https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/3857
Five-whys and evidence: parent card t_eeeeee0000000038. Short form: state CI consumed mods/core main with no pin, so an upstream push turned state red with no state commit. "Root (not caught)": nothing tested the upstream heads against state before the next state push. A mods pre-merge gate is not possible (mods main unprotected, 11 of its last 15 commits had no PR), so this canary tests the heads instead.

Change:
- scripts/ci/state_contract_dispatch.sh holds the selection logic; the workflow checks it out and runs it.
- push to main: hermes-sync-tests.yml --ref state -f core_ref=$GITHUB_SHA (mods stays at state's pin). The bb-dev-tests dispatch is unchanged.
- new hourly cron '47 * * * *' and workflow_dispatch: hermes-sync-tests.yml --ref state -f mods_ref=<hermes-mods main HEAD> -f core_ref=<core main HEAD>, no skip. The step summary records both heads, state's pins and the dispatched run.
- daily '17 11 * * *': unchanged (both workflows, no inputs).
- concurrency group stays one per event.

